From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 179] panvk: drop the single-plane retry for BC1 punch-through and BC7
Generated-by: LLM

BC1 punch-through blocks keep the dual-plane encoding instead of also
trying a single-plane line, and non-mode-6 BC7 blocks with alpha only try
it when the dual-plane error exceeds 2000. Mali-G615, 2048x2048 upload:
BC1 RGBA 57 -> 36 ms (-0.15 dB worst), real BC7 76.7 -> 64.0 ms over six
textures (-0.13 dB worst). biblioklept

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/176
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc7_astc.comp b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc7_astc.comp
index 6c8feff..0f031e7 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc7_astc.comp
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_bc7_astc.comp
@@ -976,9 +976,14 @@ uvec4 encode_block(uvec4 src, int format)
       enc_line(src, format, 8u, false, WR15, ER191, 1e30, m6, s0, s1, 3u, blk);
       return blk;
    }
+   /* A good dual-plane fit (error <= 2000) is kept as is: the single-plane
+    * retry cost 25% more time on real textures for under 0.15 dB there. */
    float e = 1e30;
-   if (!m6)
+   if (!m6) {
       e = enc_line(src, format, 12u, true, WR3, ER47, 1e30, false, vec4(0.0), vec4(0.0), 3u, blk);
+      if (e <= 2000.0)
+         return blk;
+   }
    float e2 = enc_line(src, format, 12u, false, WR15, ER47, e, m6, s0, s1, 3u, cand);
    return e2 <= e ? cand : blk;
 }
